You receive a REQUEST and a numbered list of HEADINGS.
Each heading is the title of the page or section that lists some rows: identical rows under headings of different classes are different items.
MUST: give "same" to a heading that declares its rows are items of the class asked by the REQUEST or a synonym.
MUST: give "other" to a heading that declares its rows are items of another class, "unclear" to a heading that does not declare the class of its rows.
MUST NOT: give "other" to a heading that only names the container of the rows, a menu or a greeting: that heading is "unclear".
OK: abstract example, do not copy literally: request for <ITEMS_A>; «<TITLE_OF_ITEMS_A>» → same; «<TITLE_OF_ITEMS_B>» → other; «<TITLE_OF_THE_CONTAINER>» → unclear.
ERROR: request for <ITEMS_A>; «<TITLE_OF_THE_CONTAINER>» → other.
Return ONLY a JSON object {"labels":[...]} with one label per heading, in the same order, with no prose and no placeholders.
